-- title:
--   Fixed elements are q-rescaled Γ₀(M') functions (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime which, by hypothesis, equals $2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\zeta$ be an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Write $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ for the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ and `fieldBar q M'` for the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise images of the function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H$ of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$. Let $x$ be an element of this field which is fixed by every level automorphism: for all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,(x) = x$, where `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of `fieldBar q M'` satisfying `IsLevelAutBar` — namely, for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb Q\,p_g \ne 0$, and every ring embedding $\iota : \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise $\iota$-image of $\tau$ applied to the class of $p_f/p_g$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \gamma^\sharp$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \gamma^\sharp$, for $\gamma^\sharp = \mathrm{conjElem}\,q\,\gamma$ (if no such $\tau$ exists, `levelAutBar` is the identity). The conclusion is that there exists a Laurent series $g$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying in `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M'))`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the coefficientwise images of the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb Q\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb Q\,p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_0(M')$, such that $x$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$, equals `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q g`, the Laurent series obtained from $g$ by multiplying all exponents by $q$ (substitution of $q^q$ for $q$).
--
--   This identifies the fixed field of the group of level automorphisms of the full-level field over $\Gamma_0(M')$ as the set of $q$-rescaled level-$\Gamma_0(M')$ functions, in the case $q = 2$; it is the $q = 2$ counterpart of the statement proved for $q \ge 5$. The proof combines the finiteness and generation statement for the group generated by the level automorphisms, the fact that $q$-rescaled $\Gamma_0(M')$ functions are fixed by all of them, the lower bound $q(q^2-1)$ for the order of that group and the corresponding upper bound for the relative degree, and it is used in the identification of the integral elements of the full-level field with an Igusa-type ring.
